-## How the events are emitted (determinism spine — ODN-14/ODN-15)
-
-- **PIPE_DRAWN** is emitted at the **apply tick from BOTH paths** so live and replay event streams stay byte-identical: the replay path (`core/step.odin` command loop) and the live fast-path (`app/input/exec.odin` `commit_draw`, which appends the same event at `inp.tick + 1` = the logged `apply_tick`, via a new `Input.sim_events` ref wired in `main.odin`). The T1 golden pins this: the replay of a blessed log reproduces the wire events without the consumer.
-- **NODE_SPAWNED** is emitted inside `step`'s growth branch at the growth tick. Growth is seed-derived run setup that runs identically on both paths — live and replay emit the identical event at the identical tick with zero app-side plumbing.
-- The consumer stays PURE: variant draws touch only the app-owned cosmetic Rng; the sim hash cannot move (audio on == audio off).
-
-## Immediacy (the ~50 ms acceptance)
-
-- **Wire placed:** the event is appended at input time; the consumer drains `events[audio_mark:]` once per frame → ≤ 1 frame (~16.7 ms @ 60 fps) from gesture to `PlaySound`.
-- **Spawn / crisis / arrival:** emitted inside `step`, consumed in the same frame's drain → ≤ 1 frame.
-- No new throttles: wires are player-paced (a drag gesture each), growth runs at the 80-tick (4 s) cadence — the arrival throttle exists because 30 deliveries/tick; the wire/spawn cues need none.
