+# assets/blender — the silhouette Blender pass landing zone
+
+This is where the MM-minimal silhouette pass lands (job
+`packet-plumber-v2-blender-silhouettes`).
+
+## What goes here
+
+- Your `.blend` sources, one per sprite family:
+  `house.blend`, `small_biz.blend`, `campus.blend`, `host.blend`,
+  `puck.blend` (plus `dc.blend` if you touch the unwired dc).
+- WIP renders / scratch PNGs while you sculpt. The FINAL exports go into
+  `../sprites/` with the fixed names (see below).
+
+The `.blend` files ARE committed — they are the reproducible source of the
+committed PNGs (same policy as `tools/gen_sprites.py`). Auto-backups
+(`*.blend1`) are gitignored.
+
+## Render contract (must match or the pass is rejected at fold-in)
+
+| Setting | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Canvas | 256×256, transparent PNG (RGBA) |
+| Camera | ORTHO, tilt ~49–67° (varies with the per-sprite pad — campus ≈49° steepest, pucks ≈67° shallowest) — the roof carries the read, thin outline visible all around |
+| Materials | flat emissive single-fill, sRGB→linear converted hex (`#RRGGBB` → linear for Blender color sockets) |
+| Color mgmt | Standard view transform, look None, exposure 0, gamma 1 |
+| Outline | thin dark ink `#33414F` plate at the base, ring **0.03 per side** (footprint + 0.06 total, ≈2px in-game ring) |
+| Shadows | NEVER baked — the game draws the flat ink ellipse in-engine |
+| Fills | single-fill only — no gradients, no bevels, no bloom, no 3D fake |
+
+## Export names (pinned by app/render/sprites.odin — 11 files)
+
+`house_0..3.png`, `host.png`, `dc.png`, `small_biz.png`, `campus.png`,
+`puck_1..3.png` — land in `../sprites/`. `sprites.json` (the content bboxes)
+regenerates on the next `tools/gen_sprites.py` run — do not hand-edit it.
+
+## Per-type targets
+
+See `docs/silhouette-spec.md` §1 — the fill-in-the-blanks table (footprints,
+hexes, what details to KEEP OFF). Sources: kyle-design-directions.md §3 +
+design-audit.html Q1 "Silhouette minimalism"
+(`/Users/moses/code/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/packet-plumber-v2-design-audit/`).
+
+## After you drop files here
+
+Tell the minion (or Gru). Fold-in = fill the SPEC table in
+`tools/gen_sprites.py` from your numbers (or import your .blend), re-render
+headless, regenerate `sprites.json`, then the T2 re-bless (ONE pass, cause-
+documented — goldens compare against rendered sprites).
