+# Silhouette Spec — MM-minimal sprite set (fill-in-the-blanks)
+
+Audience: the user (live in Blender) + the sprite pipeline (`tools/gen_sprites.py`).
+Target: **true MM-minimal silhouettes per node type** — flat single-fill
+rects/discs, thin dark outline, no gable step, no wash, no 3D fake.
+
+Sources of truth:
+- `kyle-design-directions.md` §3 (Node Identifiability) + §1 (Scale) —
+  preserved at
+  `/Users/moses/code/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/packet-plumber-v2-design-audit/`
+- `design-audit.html` Q1 ranked fix "Silhouette minimalism"
+- `tools/gen_sprites.py` (the pipeline; Blender 5.2.0 LTS, headless)
+
+The **pipeline is validated**: re-running the script with UNCHANGED SPEC values is
+pixel-deterministic (the pre-rework script reproduces the committed sprites
+pixel-for-pixel — decoded RGBA identical; only PNG-encoder metadata differs).
+Determinism is about re-running the SAME spec, not the new spec matching the
+old sheet — new SPEC values change geometry by design. Geometry changes flow
+through `sprites.json` content bboxes automatically — zero code churn in the
+renderer.
+
+---
+
+## 0. Render contract (every sprite)
+
+| Setting | Value | Why |
+|---|---|---|
+| Canvas | 256×256, transparent PNG (RGBA) | sprite sheet convention; renderer trims via content bbox |
+| Camera | ORTHO, tilt ~49–67° — varies with the per-sprite pad (campus steepest ≈49°, pucks shallowest ≈67°; measured from bbox projections); the roof carries the read, thin outline visible all around | the MM top-down view (7.1 canon) |
+| Materials | flat emissive single-fill, sRGB→linear converted hex | pixels land ON the canon hex; no lights, no gradients, no bevels, no bloom |
+| Color mgmt | Standard view transform, look None, exposure 0, gamma 1 | deterministic |
+| Outline | thin dark ink plate `#33414F` at the base, ring **0.03 per side** (footprint + 0.06 total, ≈2px in-game ring) | MM's defining edge |
+| Shadows | **never baked** — the game draws the flat translucent ink ellipse in-engine | Blender's hashed alpha dithers at sprite size |
+| Bbox | auto-regenerated into `assets/sprites/sprites.json` (top-down flip) | renderer trims by it |
+
+## 1. Per-type silhouette targets (the blanks to fill)
+
+### residential — `house_0..3` (gable rect)
+- **Read:** simple house. Keep the house read, **drop the roof-step detail** that
+  reads "game asset" (the chimney — the current roof-step offender).
+- **Geometry:** flat gable rect — rect footprint, ridge along the **short axis
+  (Y** in the code's orientation — the long axis is X; the +X slope is 10%
+  darker, the two-tone ridge line is the house read). No chimney, no wall
+  band, no base step, no windows/doors. (The code's gable ridge runs along Y
+  by convention — sculpt the ridge along the short side to match.)
+- **Footprint:** 0.62 × 0.56 (aspect ~1.11). In-game 1.50 tiles wide (32–40px at
+  the current zoom — KYLE §1 house:road ≈ 0.5–1.0×).
+- **Fills (4 colorways — keep the canon):**
+  coral `#E85A4A` · gold `#F2C94C` · sage `#5ECB6B` · sky `#4A9BE2`; ridge tone =
+  same hex × 0.90 shade.
+- **Outline:** yes.
+
+### small_biz — flat shop block (wide rect)
+- **Read:** a low, wide office/shop block. **No awning detail** — drop the AC
+  unit, the parapet inner panel, the cream sign band, the wall band.
+- **Geometry:** ONE flat rect, single fill + outline. Nothing else.
+- **Footprint:** 1.10 × 0.84 (aspect ~1.31 — wider than the house). In-game 1.60
+  tiles wide.
+- **Fill:** warm-stone `#9C8C6C` (KYLE §3 hue target `#A0937D` — optional swap;
+  shape carries the identity per E9.1; confirm against node-clarity palette at
+  merge).
+- **Outline:** yes.
+
+### campus — flat wide block (brick family)
+- **Read:** the biggest terminal, a wide block. **No facade lines** — drop the
+  multi-wing U/E plan, the quad strip, the pavilion, the clock tower.
+- **Geometry:** ONE flat rect, single fill + outline. Nothing else.
+- **Footprint:** 1.85 × 1.35 (aspect ~1.37 — the largest terminal). In-game 2.20
+  tiles wide.
+- **Fill:** brick `#A8503C` (KYLE §3 hue target `#8B4513` — optional swap; same
+  caveat).
+- **Outline:** yes.
+
+### content_host — flat tower-ish block (deep blue, taller aspect)
+- **Read:** a tower block — the aspect does the work. **Drop the roof markings:**
+  the play-button triangle, vent, mast, antenna sphere.
+- **Geometry:** ONE flat rect, single fill + outline, **portrait aspect** (taller
+  than wide — currently 1.14×0.88 landscape; flip to ~0.85 × 1.10 for the
+  tower read).
+- **Footprint:** ~0.85 × 1.10 (aspect ~0.77 portrait). In-game 1.75 tiles wide
+  (the drawn height follows the bbox aspect).
+- **Fill:** deep blue `#3E78D0` (KYLE §3 hue target `#4682B4` SteelBlue — optional
+  swap).
+- **Outline:** yes.
+
+### routers — `puck_1..3` (flat discs, port ring only)
+- **Read:** a machined puck. **No two-tone weight** — drop the dark under-disc,
+  the raised core, the 3D LED spheres.
+- **Geometry:** ONE flat disc (single fill) + a ring of small FLAT port dots at
+  the rim (4 / 8 / 16 by tier). Thin outline ring via the disc edge itself
+  (dark rim) OR the ink outline plate — pick one, not both.
+- **Footprint:** r 0.52 × tier scale (1.0 / 1.15 / 1.30 — keep the tier ladder).
+  In-game 1.30 tiles wide.
+- **Fills:** body `#5E6E80`, port dots `#2E8B57` (LED green; flat, not spheres).
+- **Outline:** yes (rim read).
+
+### dc (unwired — optional)
+- No catalog type maps to `dc` yet (`sprite_index_building` has no case). Same
+  flat-rect treatment for sheet consistency; zero gameplay impact. Leave as-is
+  if you want minimal churn.
+
+## 2. Where the Blender pass lands
